welcome everybody to the final  installment of gain spots next big game  series all about no man's sky so far  this week our own intrepid explorer  Daniel Dwyer has told us about the story  behind the game but gameplay within  itself and also the crazy scale of the  universe but now it's my turn and for me  there's just one question that needs to  be answered how the bloody hell does it  all work  [Music]  the way the universe is created an  inland sky the way everything is graded  is this term that we use procedural  right and we're like really picky about  that where we say it's not random  right because random to me is this like  chaotic kind of mess potentially but  procedural is like creating mathematical  formulas right and they create a result  and the result is something that's the  psyche generated on the fly by the  computer but it's a result that  hopefully looks correct looks almost  like it's been built by hand  so rather than planets just being  randomly generated and us just picking  let's say a color for a planet  right once guy be red the next guy be  blue in the next guy me green and the  next guy be black or whatever you know  we don't do that because random  generation like that results in like an  entirely red planet with an entirely red  sky and looks terrible right so we  create algorithms that do things like  decide if a planet is in the right  distance from the Sun and if it is then  it would have water and so we generate  water on that planet and that creates  rivers and it creates lakes and oceans  potentially for then it also creates  moisture in the atmosphere then that  will affect the color of the sky because  the wavelength of the light is being  diffracted in different ways to create  different colors just like in in our  world now for me the key to the whole  universe and to understanding how it all  works is not to think about what happens  when you're there but instead to think  about what happens when you're not there  take the classic philosophical thought  experiment if a tree falls in the woods  and no one is around to hear it does it  make a sound  now in the real world most of us would  answer yes to this because of the  physical makeup of our observable  reality however in no man's sky the  answer is no because if no one's around  there is no tree there is no woods there  is no planet there's just nothing  as you fly around the world in the land  sky you might encounter say a mountain  and on that mountain there might be a  tree or a particular rock beside the  tree right and that is there and that  mountain is there and that tree is there  on top of the mountain because there is  effectively a mathematical formula and  the result of that formula will always  be the same so when you go and visit  that man you will always see that tree  there and if another player goes and  visits that same mountain they will see  that exact same tree in the exact same  place but it's not stored on the disk  it's not stored in the cloud and it's  just generated there and then on the fly  when you fly away we just throw that  data away we throw away their mountains  we throw away that tree and but if you  fly back it will be there again and  because it is just following this this  this pattern so every time you go  anywhere in your man's sky you're  essentially asking the game questions  math questions and the beauty of math  questions is the answer is always the  same so if you're the chord of no man's  sky and I ask you what's 45 plus 62 for  example the answer is always 107 doesn't  matter if I ask you now or next week or  in a year from now the answer will  always be the same as Shawn put it you  can think of it as putting in inputs and  getting out outputs so when you put in  the same inputs which is just I am here  at this point in the world you will  always get the same output which is the  mountain in that exact same position or  the rock that's on top of that mountain  down to the like blade of grass it will  always be in the exact same place if  another player comes along  they you know input the same inputs they  will get the same output  [Music]  the standard way to create the stuff of  videogames is to have designers and  artists build everything by hand terrain  creatures trees buildings everything you  see has been painstakingly crafted to a  higher level of detail  Nolan Skye handles detail differently  however once again everything is  generating  we generate everything at different logs  right which is like level of detail and  and level of detail is that thing that  gamers are used to you drive around GTA  and you will see a low detailed building  suddenly pop in and become a high detail  building hours don't don't pop but we  regenerate the entire planet but like  quite a low level of detail so when you  look up and you see it kind of hanging  there and then rising you can make out  mountains and hills and canyons and if  you get into your ship and you fly into  space and fly towards that planet as you  get closer and closer to it we will  generate higher and higher detail and as  you come in to land on it we begin to  generate like the highest levels of  detail but it's not just the details  that no man's sky can generate there's  also variety pretty much everything you  see plants trees spaceships and of  course the wildlife too is all unique  each one is literally one of a kind in  the entire universe how well it's kind  of like a character creation menu so  each base piece in the world be it a  dinosaur or a tree or spaceship or  whatever has the equivalent of little  sliders for every characteristic so for  the game to create variety all it needs  to do is move them  I just might create a caste and from  that cat they will also be creating  every type of lion and every type of  tiger but also things that are much more  kind of wild and and mutated from that  all of those creatures all of the ships  that you see in the sky and the  freighters and things like that they're  all following what we would call like a  fractal pattern so that means that  creatures will go down to the water and  drink some water and come back up to  higher ground and perhaps eat some grass  and go for a sleep so that some  creatures will only come out at night  all of those sort of things and they're  just again following like a mathematical  formula and so we don't simulate them  and that means that if you're on a  planet and you see a creature doing  something like that and then you fly  away and you come back it will be a  little bit further along that pattern  basically  the time I spent talking to Sean one  thing struck me over and over again  about the world they're creating due to  the layers and layers of simple  algorithms they've created a complicated  and mathematically chaotic system more  so than the sum of its parts and for me  this is the perfect example of chaos  theory changing just one thing in the  code has inherently unpredictable  results and this is what the challenge  that they need to overcome but also what  gets me so excited about the future of  no man's sky  [Music]  so I will make a rule that say there  should be little flowers around the base  of a tree right and I'll think that's a  good rule and then I like propagate that  to the main branch and suddenly there  are flowers around the base of every  tree unlike every planet right and  that's cool except it has like horrible  mouth guards right and I realized that  I'm an idiot that I'm not a god and this  was a terrible rule and suddenly all the  creatures are going crazy and they're  trying to eat around the base of trees  and they're eating flowers and things  like that and and so yeah you break the  universe horribly because you have this  this ridiculous power you've got loads  of simple rules they all each has a  cause and effect but you find it  impossible to predict what they're gonna  result in because there's a whole bunch  of even just with like half a dozen  rules it suddenly becomes really hard to  predict what's gonna happen  [Music]

